# Adjectives Content Map

Adjective agreement patterns showing how adjectives match nouns in gender, case, and number.

## Route

```
/reference/adjectives
```

## Data Source

Static content from constants:
- `@/constants/adjectives` - ADJECTIVE_PARADIGMS, ADJECTIVE_ENDINGS_QUICK_REF, ADJECTIVE_AGREEMENT_EXAMPLES, COMMON_ADJECTIVES, ADJECTIVE_MISTAKES

## Components

- `AdjectivesSection` - Main adjectives content
- `AdjectiveEndingsTable` - Quick reference endings
- `AgreementExamplesCard` - Article + adjective + noun examples
- `AdjectiveParadigmCard` - Full paradigm for a pattern
- `CommonAdjectivesCard` - High-frequency vocabulary

---

## Section: Adjectives

<section id="adjectives">
<purpose>Words that describe nouns, agreeing in gender, case, and number</purpose>

### Key Insight

<insight title="Adjectives copy the noun">
Match the article's gender and case. The adjective ending follows the same pattern as nouns.

<expanded-example label="What this means">
Look at the article. The adjective uses the same gender, case, and number as the noun it describes.

| Greek | Analysis |
|-------|----------|
| ο καλός φίλος | all masculine nominative |
| τον καλό φίλο | all masculine accusative, drop the -ς |
</expanded-example>
</insight>

### Word Order

<alert variant="info">
Word Order: Greek adjectives usually come **before** the noun: ο καλός φίλος (the good friend), not *ο φίλος καλός.
</alert>

### Adjective Endings Quick Reference

<paradigm title="Standard adjective endings (-ος, -η, -ο pattern)">

**Singular:**
| Case | Masculine | Feminine | Neuter |
|------|-----------|----------|--------|
| Nom | -ος | -η | -ο |
| Acc | -ο | -η | -ο |
| Gen | -ου | -ης | -ου |

**Plural:**
| Case | Masculine | Feminine | Neuter |
|------|-----------|----------|--------|
| Nom | -οι | -ες | -α |
| Acc | -ους | -ες | -α |
| Gen | -ων | -ων | -ων |
</paradigm>

### Agreement in Action

<examples title="Article + Adjective + Noun">

**Nominative (subject):**
| Greek | English | Gender |
|-------|---------|--------|
| ο καλός φίλος | the good friend | masculine |
| η καλή φίλη | the good friend | feminine |
| το καλό παιδί | the good child | neuter |

**Accusative (object):**
| Greek | English | Gender |
|-------|---------|--------|
| τον καλό φίλο | the good friend | masculine |
| την καλή φίλη | the good friend | feminine |
| το καλό παιδί | the good child | neuter |
</examples>

### Main Pattern (covers ~80% of adjectives)

<paradigm pattern="-ος, -η, -ο" title="Standard adjective pattern" frequency="very common">
<example>
καλός / καλή / καλό = good
</example>

**Masculine:**
| Case | Singular | Plural |
|------|----------|--------|
| Nom | καλός | καλοί |
| Acc | καλό | καλούς |
| Gen | καλού | καλών |

**Feminine:**
| Case | Singular | Plural |
|------|----------|--------|
| Nom | καλή | καλές |
| Acc | καλή | καλές |
| Gen | καλής | καλών |

**Neuter:**
| Case | Singular | Plural |
|------|----------|--------|
| Nom | καλό | καλά |
| Acc | καλό | καλά |
| Gen | καλού | καλών |
</paradigm>

### Common Adjectives

<vocabulary title="High-frequency adjectives (all follow -ος/-η/-ο pattern)" colour="honey">
| Greek | English |
|-------|---------|
| καλός | good |
| κακός | bad |
| μεγάλος | big |
| μικρός | small |
| νέος | new, young |
| παλιός | old |
| ωραίος | nice, beautiful |
| άσχημος | ugly |
| εύκολος | easy |
| δύσκολος | difficult |
| ακριβός | expensive |
| φτηνός | cheap |
| ζεστός | hot, warm |
| κρύος | cold |
| γρήγορος | fast |
| αργός | slow |
</vocabulary>

<collapsible title="Other Adjective Patterns" colour="olive">

<paradigm pattern="-ύς, -ιά, -ύ" title="Deep/heavy pattern" frequency="common">
<example>
βαρύς / βαριά / βαρύ = heavy
</example>
<tip>Notice the accent shift in feminine</tip>

**Forms:** βαρύς, βαριά, βαρύ (heavy); ελαφρύς, ελαφριά, ελαφρύ (light)
</paradigm>

<paradigm pattern="-ής, -ής, -ές" title="Two-ending pattern" frequency="less common">
<example>
διεθνής / διεθνής / διεθνές = international
</example>
<tip>Masculine and feminine are identical</tip>

**Forms:** διεθνής (m/f), διεθνές (n) - international; ευγενής (m/f), ευγενές (n) - polite
</paradigm>

</collapsible>

<collapsible title="Common Adjective Mistakes" colour="terracotta">
| Wrong | Correct | Explanation |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| ο καλή φίλος | ο καλός φίλος | Adjective must match masculine noun |
| τον καλός φίλο | τον καλό φίλο | Accusative drops the -ς |
| η μεγάλο σπίτι | το μεγάλο σπίτι | σπίτι is neuter, needs neuter article and adjective |
| ο νέο αυτοκίνητο | το νέο αυτοκίνητο | αυτοκίνητο is neuter |
</collapsible>
</section>

---

## Content Guidelines

1. **Key insight first** - "Adjectives copy the noun" is the core principle
2. **Quick reference prominent** - Endings table for fast lookup
3. **Agreement examples** - Show full phrases, not isolated words
4. **Main pattern focus** - The -ος/-η/-ο pattern covers most adjectives
5. **Common vocabulary** - Practical adjectives learners will use
6. **Other patterns collapsible** - Don't overwhelm beginners
7. **Connect to practice** - CTA links to /practice/speed?focus=adjectives
